logo-discord.svg, logo-slack.svg, logo-mattermost.svg, logo-telegram.svg
and logo-pushover.svg (the notification channels), and logo-git.svg,
logo-github.svg, logo-gitlab.svg, logo-docker.svg, logo-postgres.svg,
logo-mysql.svg, logo-mariadb.svg, logo-mongodb.svg, logo-redis.svg,
logo-clickhouse.svg, logo-cloudflared.svg, logo-minio.svg, logo-n8n.svg,
logo-uptime-kuma.svg and logo-wordpress.svg (what the Add resource page
offers) are from the selfh.st icon collection
(https://selfh.st/icons, https://github.com/selfhst/icons), which is
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Changed here: each style attribute is written as the presentation
attributes it stands for (style="fill:#5865f2" is fill="#5865f2"), since
the dashboard's content security policy drops a style attribute, and a
<style> element of classes is written onto what had the class, for the
same reason. Nothing else of a file is changed.

The collection has no SVG of three:

logo-ghost.svg is the outline from Simple Icons
(https://simpleicons.org, CC0 1.0), in Ghost's own black on a white disc.

logo-keydb.svg and logo-dragonfly.svg are the outlines from Coolify's
public/svgs (https://github.com/coollabsio/coolify, Apache License 2.0),
which draws them in one colour. Changed here: the colours are those of
each owner's own icon (KeyDB's favicon; the two ends of the gradient in
Dragonfly's logo), and the editor's metadata is removed.

The logos of the services the catalogue was filled with from Coolify's and
Dokploy's (the keys listed in ../../catalog/services.SOURCES, each with
where its logo is from) were put here by tools/catalog:

- "selfhst:<file>" is from the selfh.st icon collection named above
  (CC BY 4.0).
- "coolify:<file>" is from Coolify's public/svgs
  (https://github.com/coollabsio/coolify, Apache License 2.0).
- "dokploy:<file>" is from the blueprint of that service in Dokploy's
  templates (https://github.com/Dokploy/templates, MIT License);
  "dokploy:<folder>/<file>" is from another blueprint's folder there, of
  the same service under another name.
- "dashboard:<file>" is from Dashboard Icons
  (https://github.com/homarr-labs/dashboard-icons, Apache License 2.0).
- "svgl:<file>" is from svgl (https://github.com/pheralb/svgl, MIT
  License).
- "simple:<file>" is the outline from Simple Icons
  (https://simpleicons.org, CC0 1.0), in the one colour that collection
  gives for the brand.

A file whose name ends in "-dark" is that collection's drawing of the logo
for a light page.

Changed here, in each of them: a style attribute and a <style> element of
classes are written as presentation attributes, as above, a rule that
holds only on a dark page is left out, and comments, titles, descriptions
and an editor's own metadata are removed. A service's logo is a file of at
most 6 KB wherever one of its files is that small, as it stands or with
the coordinates of its paths written with fewer decimals (to a
ten-thousandth of the drawing's size); a service with no such file has one
of at most 20 KB, written with fewer decimals. A logo that could not be
written this way or is larger than that was not taken as a drawing.

A logo-<key>.webp file is a picture of a logo, for a service whose logo
none of these has as a drawing the dashboard can show. services.SOURCES
names the file it was made of, as above: "selfhst:<file>.webp" and
"dashboard:<file>.webp" are those collections' own pictures of the logo;
a ".png", ".jpg", ".jpeg", ".webp" or ".ico" file of Coolify's or
Dokploy's is the logo that catalogue shows for the service; an ".svg"
file is a drawing that has text, a link or a picture in it, or is larger
than 20 KB. Changed here: what is around the logo is cut off (a
transparent edge, or white paper), the picture is made at most 96 pixels
a side, never larger than its file, and written as WebP of at most 6 KB.

A logo that is drawn in white, for a dark page, is shown on a dark square
with round corners (#1f2328): a drawing inside an SVG file that is the
square, a picture on a square that is part of the picture. Nothing of the
logo itself is changed.

Each logo is a trademark of its owner and is used only to name that
owner's service.

logo-email.svg and logo-webhook.svg are musdash's own. The outline of the
webhook mark is Hugeicons' (MIT licence, ../ui/icons.LICENSE).
